## Project identity
This is the Hawk Merchandising Web Portal — a B2B platform for outsourced logo and
merchandising design. Clients submit work, admins coordinate designers, billing runs
in USD (clients) and PKR (designer payouts).

---

## Tech stack

### Backend
- Runtime: .NET 8 (ASP.NET Core)
- Architecture: Clean Architecture — 4 layers in strict dependency order:
  Domain → Application → Infrastructure → API
- ORM: EF Core 8 + Pomelo.EntityFrameworkCore.MySql
- Database: MySQL 8
- Cache: Redis 6+ (StackExchange.Redis)
- Auth: JWT Bearer + HttpOnly cookies (ldp_access, ldp_refresh) + CSRF double-submit (ldp_csrf / X-XSRF-TOKEN)
- Background jobs: Hangfire (Redis storage in prod, in-memory in dev)
- Real-time: SignalR hub at /hubs/notifications (Redis backplane in prod)
- PDF: QuestPDF
- HTTP resilience: Polly
- Logging: Serilog (structured)
- Mapping: AutoMapper
- Password hashing: BCrypt
- Testing: xUnit + Moq + WebApplicationFactory

### Frontend
- Framework: Angular 17
- UI library: PrimeNG 17 — NO Material UI ever
- Charts: ApexCharts (primary), Chart.js (legacy — consolidating to ApexCharts)
- Real-time: @microsoft/signalr
- Reactive: RxJS
- State: Services + RxJS (no NgRx)
- Unit tests: Karma + Jasmine
- E2E tests: Playwright

