## Coding style preferences

### C# (.NET)
- Use `async/await` throughout — no `.Result` or `.Wait()`
- Use `CancellationToken` parameters on all async public methods
- Use record types for DTOs where possible
- Prefer `ILogger<T>` injected via constructor
- Use `[RequirePermission("PermissionName")]` for granular permission checks
- XML doc comments on all public interfaces and service methods
- Guard clauses at the top of methods — fail fast, fail early

### Angular / TypeScript
- Use typed observables — never `any` unless absolutely unavoidable
- Use `OnPush` change detection on new components
- Services are singleton (providedIn: 'root') unless feature-scoped
- Unsubscribe in ngOnDestroy or use `takeUntilDestroyed()`
- All API calls go through a typed service — never HttpClient directly in components
- PrimeNG components only — no custom UI from scratch if PrimeNG has it

### General
- No magic strings — use constants or enums
- No commented-out code in commits
- Every new file gets a corresponding test file
- Ops scripts (PowerShell) use variables at the top for all configurable paths

