## What NOT to do — ever

- Do not add NgRx (no Redux pattern — RxJS services are the state solution)
- Do not add MediatR or CQRS patterns (not in scope)
- Do not add Angular Material or any UI library other than PrimeNG
- Do not edit anything in Backend/ outside of Backend/src/ (legacy folders excluded)
- Do not expose Swagger in Staging or Production environments
- Do not hardcode any environment-specific URL, key, or credential
- Do not set order status directly — always use OrderStatusStateMachine
- Do not expose designer identity to client DTOs or vice versa
- Do not create migrations manually — always use `dotnet ef migrations add`
- Do not use `.Result` or `.Wait()` on async calls (deadlock risk in ASP.NET)

